# PART 3 — 10% PROMOTIONAL OFFER RULE

I am currently running a 10% discount promotion on ALL 74 STUDIO orders.

This must be incorporated into the 74 STUDIO Sales Intelligence conversation-generation system.

## 3.1 Promotional rule

Whenever an artist shows genuine interest in a service, package, price, project or potential booking, naturally mention the current 10% discount.

Examples of genuine buying interest:

- Asking about pricing.
- Asking about packages.
- Asking how much a project costs.
- Asking about booking.
- Asking about project availability.
- Asking about deliverables.
- Confirming that they need a service.
- Discussing a project they want to start.
- Comparing options before purchasing.
- Indicating that they want to work with 74 STUDIO.

The AI must include the 10% promotional offer in every promising sales conversation, not merely in the first response.

If the artist asks a follow-up question later in the same buying conversation, make sure the promotion is not forgotten.

However:

- Do not insert the discount into unrelated casual conversations.
- Do not force it into every single message.
- Do not repeatedly announce it in consecutive messages when it has already been clearly communicated and is not relevant to the current response.
- Do not make it sound desperate or pushy.

## 3.2 Example promotional wording

Use natural Discord-style language.

For example:

"btw, we're currently running a 10% discount on all orders, so it's a pretty good time to get the visuals sorted."

Or:

"also, we've got 10% off all orders at the moment, so that applies to this project too."

Generate variations naturally instead of repeating the same sentence.

## 3.3 Discount calculations and price integrity

The promotion applies to all orders, including custom-quote services.

Rules:
- Never invent an expiration date.
- Never invent a coupon code.
- Never invent additional promotion conditions.
- Never claim that the promotion is ending soon.
- Never create artificial urgency.
- Do not change the official base prices in the knowledge base.
- Preserve the "+" on all starting prices.
- For custom projects, explain that the 10% discount applies to the confirmed order quote.
- Only calculate a discounted amount when the underlying price and applicable scope are sufficiently clear.
- Clearly distinguish starting prices from final quotes.

Make the promotion configurable in a small settings section so I can update or deactivate it later without changing the AI system prompt.

Initial settings:
- Promotion status: Active.
- Discount: 10%.
- Scope: All orders.
- Expiration: Not specified.
- Coupon code: None specified.

