## 5.5 Security

- Enable RLS on exposed tables.
- Ensure workspace and user isolation.
- Keep Supabase secret keys on the backend only.
- Never expose service-role or secret keys in frontend code.
- Preserve encryption for Instagram and YouTube credentials.
- Keep encryption keys in server-side secrets.
- Never log OAuth tokens or provider API keys.
- Validate backend request payloads.
- Implement proper file upload limits and access controls.

## 5.6 Migration safety

Use a staged migration.

1. Back up all existing data.
2. Inspect and inventory existing sources.
3. Create Supabase schema.
4. Configure Firebase JWT trust and RLS.
5. Import data into a staging environment.
6. Verify record counts and relationships.
7. Migrate files and verify references.
8. Test reads and writes.
9. Switch application data access.
10. Perform controlled production cutover.
11. Keep the old sources untouched until verification and recovery requirements are met.

The migration importer must be idempotent.

Do not create permanent uncontrolled dual writes.

Provide a tested rollback procedure.

Do not delete Firebase or Firestore resources as part of this migration.

